 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Decorator:** `needs_app_scope` in `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It wraps a callback so it runs inside the app context.\n\n- If you register the command under `app.cli` or `bundle.cli` (an `AppGroup`, e.g. `@app.cli.command()`), it's applied automatically, so you don't need to add it.\n- For a standalone `click` command, add `@needs_app_scope` yourself.\n\n**App loading:** `LaunchInfo` in `src/tessel/cli.py:293`. Its `load_app()` (line 333) loads and caches the app. `needs_app_scope` calls it through `ctx.ensure_object(LaunchInfo).load_app()`.\n\n`TesselGroup` (line 531) is the top-level CLI group and also loads the app via `LaunchInfo`.",
